 },
 "summary": "A family of thick film chip resistors built to take electrostatic surges better than ordinary metal film chips: ERJPA2 (0402), ERJPA3 and ERJP03 (0603), ERJP06 (0805), ERJP08 and ERJPM8 (1206) and ERJP14 (1210). Power ratings run from 0.20 W to 0.66 W, limiting element voltage from 50 V to 500 V, values from 1 Ω to 10 MΩ in ±0.5 %, ±1 % and ±5 % tolerances, over a −55 to +155 °C category range. ERJPM8 is the high-value 1206 part, 1.02 MΩ to 10 MΩ at ±1 % and ±100 ppm/K. The family is AEC-Q200 qualified (Grade 0, ERJPA2 Grade 1), RoHS compliant, and solders by reflow or flow.",
