 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "A metal glaze thick film element sits on an alumina substrate under a protective coat. Each end carries a three-layer termination: inner, middle and outer electrode."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Power derating",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Parts rated at an ambient temperature keep full power up to their rated ambient (70 °C for most, 105 °C for ERJPA3 at 0.25 W) and fall to zero at 155 °C; ERJP06, ERJP08 and ERJPM8 fall to 50 % at 125 °C on the way. Parts rated at terminal temperature keep full power up to the rated terminal temperature (100, 130, 115 and 125 °C for ERJPA2, ERJPA3, ERJP06 and ERJP08/PM8) and reach zero at 155 °C. For ERJP14, provided its temperature does not exceed 155 °C, derating may begin at 125 °C instead of 70 °C. In every case the part's own temperature must remain under the upper category temperature."
  },
  {
   "topic": "ESD robustness",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Under the ESD test (±3 kV from 150 pF for 0603 and up, ±1 kV from 100 pF for 0402) the ERJP parts shift by about 3.5 % or less across 10 Ω to 1 MΩ, where the standard ERJ thick film chips of the same size shift by up to about 25 % near 10 kΩ. The curves are reference data."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "Reflow and flow soldering both suit the part. Its resistance-to-soldering-heat test is 270 °C for 10 s. Preheat so the part is within 100 °C of the solder, and keep any quench bath within 100 °C of the part. With an iron, preheat the part, keep the tip off the body, and finish within 3 s at a tip temperature of 350 °C or below. Use rosin flux; avoid strongly halogenated, strongly acidic, water-soluble or fluoride-bearing fluxes, and keep flux off the body. Very low values can shift with solder volume."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Board and handling",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "The chip is thin and chips or cracks under impact, tweezers or board flexing: keep it away from break-off lines and large holes, support the board when placing other parts, and split panels with a jig. A removed part is not to be reused. ESD can shift the value during handling; 40 % to 60 % RH, wrist straps and grounded mats are given as measures. Resin potting or coating stresses the electrodes and is outside guaranteed use."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Storage",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "Store at 5 to 35 °C and 45 % to 85 % RH, out of sunlight and corrosive gases (Cl2, H2S, NH3, SO2, NOx), and use within one year of delivery."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Standards",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Reference standards: IEC 60115-8, JIS C 5201-8 and JEITA RC-2134C. AEC-Q200 compliant and RoHS compliant."
  }
 ],
